  "revision_changes_vs_v3": "V1 (2ac3ad0) rejected by the owner: too many borders. V2 (73a2823) merged the sky, both lattice doors and the moon/cloud layer into one back plate, shrank the clear rim 2.5 -> 1.0 mm and rendered clear acrylic see-through in the assembly preview. V3 (657a484) recomposed the scene but the owner prefers V2 (\"v2가 낫다고 한거야\"), so V4 starts from the V2 design: the V2 composition is restored unchanged (sky 90 mm, doors 85 mm, moon/clouds 60 mm, tree plate 72 mm at x=112, serpent 55 mm at x=115, character 84 mm at x=170 on row 12) as the base; the owner's two V4 requests are applied on top in the next step.",
  "preview_rendering": "clear acrylic see-through on a dark mauve ground: plate bodies unfilled, one 0.26 mm lit-edge stroke per plate, tabs clipped at the shoulder (inside the slots); base slab shows its front side band",
